Feature 1 — Anchor defense. lock_draft picks anchors by matching words in the utterance against symbols. It has now failed three times on real work: "tabs" matched tab characters in a parser, "fold/mark" matched the TypeScript engine for a SwiftUI task, "element" matched parser symbols instead of a UI control. Every time, a careful agent had to fix the budget by hand. Fix: before proposing a budget, the draft must defend each anchor — for every anchor, report which file it came from and why that territory matches the utterance — and when all anchors land in a different language/directory than the user's words suggest (e.g. UI words but parser files), flag "low confidence — confirm territory with the human" at the top of the draft.